TASK-132.11 runtime harness: the tab group stripe on sidebar rows and the
group line on the hover card. Temporary code, never committed to Detour/.
Apply, build, run, revert:

    git apply docs/harness/task132.11-harness.patch
    xcodegen generate
    xcodebuild -scheme Detour -configuration Debug -derivedDataPath .derived build
    # 1. Seed phase (fresh data dir): eight data: URL tabs, Charlie|Delta split, saved.
    #    New tabs open at the top, so the list is Hotel, Golf, Foxtrot, Echo,
    #    Charlie|Delta, Bravo, Alpha.
    DETOUR_DATA_DIR=DetourVerify13211 DETOUR_VERIFY_DIR="$OUT" DETOUR_VERIFY_PHASE=seed \
        .derived/Build/Products/Debug/Detour.app/Contents/MacOS/Detour &
    # wait for "done" in $OUT/verify-seed.log, kill that pid, then seed the groups:
    DB="$HOME/Library/Application Support/DetourVerify13211/browser.db"
    SP=$(sqlite3 "$DB" "select spaceID from tab limit 1")
    G1=11111111-1111-4111-8111-111111111111; G2=22222222-2222-4222-8222-222222222222
    sqlite3 "$DB" "insert into tabGroup (id, spaceID, title, color, isCollapsed, sortOrder)
        values ('$G1','$SP','Research','blue',0,0), ('$G2','$SP','','purple',0,1);
        update tab set tabGroupID='$G1' where title in ('Echo','Charlie','Delta','Bravo');
        update tab set tabGroupID='$G2' where title='Golf';"
    # 2. Check phase: same data dir, DETOUR_VERIFY_PHASE=check. Each "SHOOT <name>
    #    <window> <panel>" line in $OUT/verify-check.log is a cue to run
    #    `screencapture -x -o -l<window>` (and -l<panel> when it is not 0) from
    #    the shell; the harness pauses 1.5-2 s after each. It also writes an
    #    in-process sidebar PNG (layer.render) per cue. Ends with "done".
    git apply -R docs/harness/task132.11-harness.patch && xcodegen generate

The check phase logs every visible tab row (height, stripe colour, title and
continuation, the stripe's frame in row coordinates, the row's selection rect,
whether the stripe clears it, TabGroupColorView count and the accessibility
label), in light then dark: at rest, with the split row selected, and while
hovering Bravo (Research), Golf (unnamed) and Foxtrot (ungrouped) with the
hover card's texts and dot. Then it drives TabStore live: recolour and rename
Research, ungroup Echo, create a group on Hotel, add Echo back, name the
unnamed group, move Bravo out; after each it logs the rows and whether every
row still has the same cell instance (no reload).

